[ti:Daisy Bell (Bicycle Built for Two)]
[ar:Edward M. Favor]
[au:Harry Dacre]
[length:02:14]
[00:07.00]There is a flower within my heart,
[00:10.50]Daisy, Daisy!
[00:14.00]Planted one day by a glancing dart,
[00:17.50]Planted by Daisy Bell!
[00:21.00]Whether she loves me or loves me not,
[00:24.50]Sometimes it's hard to tell;
[00:28.00]Yet I am longing to share the lot
[00:31.50]Of beautiful Daisy Bell!
[00:37.00]Daisy, Daisy,
[00:40.50]Give me your answer, do!
[00:44.00]I'm half crazy,
[00:47.50]All for the love of you!
[00:51.00]It won't be a stylish marriage,
[00:54.50]I can't afford a carriage,
[00:58.00]But you'll look sweet upon the seat
[01:01.50]Of a bicycle built for two!
[01:05.50]
[01:09.00]We will go "tandem" as man and wife,
[01:12.80]Daisy, Daisy!
[01:16.30]"Ped'ling" away down the road of life,
[01:19.80]I and my Daisy Bell!
[01:23.30]When the road's dark we can both despise
[01:27.00]P'licemen and "lamps" as well;
[01:30.50]There are "bright lights" in the dazzling eyes
[01:34.00]Of beautiful Daisy Bell!
[01:39.30]Daisy, Daisy,
[01:42.80]Give me your answer, do!
[01:46.30]I'm half crazy,
[01:49.80]All for the love of you!
[01:53.30]It won't be a stylish marriage,
[01:56.80]I can't afford a carriage,
[02:00.30]But you'll look sweet upon the seat
[02:03.80]Of a bicycle built for two!
[02:07.50]
